666437475,2026-10-14 00:23:25,TooLongToLose,2024-12-04,175,2,,"The $CRWV conundrum is that from 6/30/2026 to 12/31/2027 the company will have to outlay nearly $90B in cash on just the following NEEDS: - $3.4B in lease payments - $10.6B in principal debt payments - $4.5B in interest expense - $70B in capital expenditures In other words… $88.5B in just those cash outlays in the next 18mo when mgmt has only guided to a top line 2026 exit ARR figure of &lt; $20B. Virtually none of that actually gets converted to cash flow from ops mind you as margins are razor thin. In other words… they’ll be issuing even MORE capital, and a F*CK TON at that. What’s the problem with doing that you ask? Well, notes they issued at a 9.625% coupon just a few months ago have already puked with buyers now demanding a whopping 15% yield to take the paper. Share price decline reflects the harsh reality of a very irresponsible mgmt team (whose dumping shares like no tomorrow). $NBIS $IREN"
