666783446,2026-10-17 23:44:39,SpartanTradeAlerts,2026-10-16,4,3,,"The $CRWV debate this week was never really about demand. Shares lost about a quarter of their value, the worst week in 11 months, after a chart of its bond yields went viral on X. The 2032 notes pushed toward 15%, credit protection spiked to levels implying roughly a 60% chance of default within five years, and a one word reply from Elon Musk helped the chart travel. The other side is just as large. Backlog sits near $104B, Q2 revenue doubled to about $2.6B, and CEO Michael Intrator called the reaction irrational, saying contracted work covers what is owed. Dan Ives made a similar case Friday, calling the selloff a false narrative. Watch Monday whether credit calms first. With roughly $50B in obligations and $35B to $39B in planned spending this year, equity likely follows the bond market here, not the other way around."
